198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,4340,1657,8153,10747,374,894,6716,315,15279,11067,315,264,5792,12371,6113,448,3108,315,220,21,8153,30,17399,697,4226,304,44548,17855,1352,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nHow many units apart is any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with side of 6 units? Express your answer in simplest radical form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b0c864f27287856360fda3e11656a529cc49721449efde5d17ce3ded82e3d3d5"},"seconds":19.871667623519897,"seed":970238523449491175,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we will first analyze the geometry of a regular hexagon and then calculate the distance between any pair of parallel sides.\n\n1. **Understanding the Regular Hexagon**:\n   - A regular hexagon has 6 equal sides, each of 6 units in this case.\n   - It can be divided into 6 equilateral triangles, each with a side length of 6 units.\n\n2. **Height of an Equilateral Triangle**:\n   - Consider one of the equilateral triangles that make up the hexagon.\n   - The side length of the triangle is 6 units.\n   - The height \\( h \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) is given by the formula:\n     \\[\n     h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s\n     \\]\n   - Substituting \\( s = 6 \\):\n     \\[\n     h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Distance between Parallel Sides of the Hexagon**:\n   - In a regular hexagon, the distance between any pair of parallel sides is twice the height of one of the equilateral triangles.\n   - Therefore, the distance \\( d \\) between any pair of parallel sides is:\n     \\[\n     d = 2 \\times 3\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\n     \\]\n\nThus, the distance between any pair of parallel sides of the hexagon is \\(\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
